RA AI-assisted development", "engineering leadership Africa", "fractional CTO Africa"], "faq": [["Should AI agents be allowed to approve code?", "Only for changes that are low risk by definition, such as documentation, dependency patches with passing tests or copy changes, and only where a policy file states this explicitly. Code that moves money, handles identity or touches personal data should always need a human owner's approval."], ["How do you stop AI review becoming a rubber stamp?", "Keep humans accountable for high-risk paths through code ownership rules, compare agent findings with human reviews during a trial period, and measure change failure rate and recovery time alongside throughput."], ["What evidence do auditors and partners need?", "For each merge: who or what reviewed it, who approved it, which checks ran and which policy allowed it. Repository rules, code owners and exported audit logs together provide that trail."]], "related": ["/regions/", "/fractional-cto/", "/ai-architect/"], "citations": [{"title": "Anthropic launches Claude Ship, letting AI agents review, fix, and approve code changes", "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/23/anthropic-launches-claude-ship-letting-ai-agents-review-fix-and-approve-code-changes/", "publisher": "TechCrunch", "date": "23 Nov 2026"}, {"title": "Claude Ship gives AI a seat on both sides of code review", "url": "https://www.helpnetsecurity.com/2026/11/24/anthropic-claude-ship-beta/", "publisher": "Help Net Security", "date": "24 Nov 2026"}, {"title": "About code owners", "url": "https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners", "publisher": "GitHub Docs"}, {"title": "About rulesets", "url": "https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/configuring-branches-and-merges-in-your-repository/managing-rulesets/about-rulesets", "publisher": "GitHub Docs"}, {"title": "DORA research", "url": "https://dora.dev/research/", "publisher": "DORA"}]